From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:30:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(settings): the engine is selectable in the Settings UI

The `engine` setting has existed since Phase 4 but only in JSON - it had no
EnumMappings entry and no control, so the one thing that makes this fork
different was reachable only by hand-editing settings.json.

It now appears in Profiles -> Advanced as "Terminal engine", above path
translation, with the same SettingContainer treatment every other enum setting
gets: inheritance, reset-to-default, and the override source.

Five places, because that is what a profile enum costs in this codebase:
EnumMappings (idl/h/cpp) so the strings come from the same JSON mapper the
serializer uses, the view model's projected setting and bindable enum, the IDL
so the XAML compiler can see ClearEngine and friends, the XAML itself, and the
resource strings.

The help text says what the JSON cannot: changing it affects new tabs and panes,
because a pane keeps the engine it was opened with.

WT suites unchanged; this is editor UI, which they do not reach.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
